U='https://www.dot.nd.gov/sites/www/files/documents/Standard%20Specifications/2023%20Standard%20Specifications.pdf'
S='North Dakota DOT Standard Specifications for Road and Bridge Construction, 2023, Sections 714, 722, 724 (read 2026-11-20)'
add('spec-nd-pipe-1','ND','North Dakota NDDOT culverts and storm drains: 6-inch lifts, 90 percent, 95 percent mandrel (Section 714)',
"North Dakota (NDDOT 2023 Standard Specifications, Section 714, Culverts, Storm Drains, Edgedrains, and Underdrains). Bedding is tamped under both haunches up to 15 percent of the pipe height with hand-held air tampers (714.04 A.4). Backfill in lifts of 6 inches or less; aggregate backfill compacted to at least 90 percent of maximum dry density at 2 points below to 3 points above optimum moisture (714.04 A.10 and A.11). Cover before equipment crosses: the book gives no number and sends you to the pipe maker's recommendation (714.04 A.12). Deflection test: metal and thermoplastic pipe under mainline and paved crossroads is tested at least 30 days after installation with a nine-point mandrel at least 95 percent of the inside diameter; pipe the mandrel will not pass is replaced (714.04 A.8). Concrete pipe joints are wrapped in geotextile. Jacked steel pipe: bore without water, start within 0.1 foot of staked grade, and stay within 1/2 foot of line and grade (714.04 C). Manholes and inlets (722): backfill lifts of 6 inches or less at 90 percent. Water and sewer lines (724): bedding up the sides to one-third of the pipe diameter, backfill in 6-inch loose lifts.",S,U,'2023')

U='https://www.dot.state.oh.us/Divisions/ConstructionMgt/OnlineDocs/Specifications/2013CMS/600/611.htm'
S='Ohio DOT Construction and Material Specifications, Item 611, 2013 online edition (read 2026-11-20). The current book is the 2023 C&MS with yearly updates, which was not read.'
add('spec-oh-pipe-1','OH','Ohio ODOT pipe culverts and sewers: installation plan, 7.5 percent deflection, 30 to 90 day inspection (Item 611)',
"Ohio (ODOT Construction and Material Specifications, Item 611, Pipe Culverts, Sewers, Drains, and Drainage Structures). These numbers are from the 2013 online edition; the current 2023 book was not checked, so treat them as not confirmed for a current job and read Item 611 in the contract's edition. In Item 611 the contractor's installation plan sets trench dimensions, bedding, lift thickness and compaction (611.04, 611.06); rock or unsuitable material is removed at least 6 inches below the pipe and replaced with structural backfill; if no bedding is used, the middle third of the bed is loosened. With low-strength mortar bedding, the mortar backfill is carried at least 6 inches over the conduit. Performance inspection (611.12): for runs over 20 feet, 30 to 90 days after finished grade, with 5 workdays notice to the Engineer and a video record. Metal and plastic conduit is repaired or replaced if the mandrel will not pass or the laser profile shows more than 7.5 percent deflection (611.13). Sanitary concrete pipe joints are tested under ASTM C969 or C1103. Structure inverts must be within 0.1 foot or 5 percent of the pipe diameter, whichever is greater (611.14).",S,U,'2013 online (current book is 2023)','low')

U='https://www.dot.nv.gov/doing-business/about-ndot/ndot-divisions/engineering/design/standard-specifications-and-plans'
S='Nevada DOT, Standard Specifications, Standard Plans, and Design Guides page (edition list read 2026-11-20; the 2024 book itself would not open)'
add('spec-nv-edition-1','NV','Nevada NDOT Standard Specifications: current edition and where pipe work is covered',
"Nevada (NDOT Standard Specifications for Road and Bridge Construction). NDOT lists the 2024 edition as current. The numbers for pipe culverts, structure excavation and backfill in the 2024 book are not confirmed in this library because the file would not open; get them from the book on NDOT's Standard Specifications and Plans page or from the NDOT Specifications office. In the Las Vegas valley, city, county and water district work normally follows the Uniform Standard Specifications and Drawings for Clark County instead, and in the Reno area the Standard Specifications for Public Works Construction (the Orange Book), each with the agency's own amendments. Your contract says which book governs.",S,U,'2024','low')

U='https://connect.udot.utah.gov/business/standards/'
S='UDOT Standard Specifications and Standard Drawings page (edition list read 2026-11-20; the books are in an online folder that would not open)'
add('spec-ut-edition-1','UT','Utah UDOT Standard Specifications: editions listed and where city work differs',
"Utah (UDOT Standard Specifications). UDOT's standards page lists yearly books, with 2027 the newest listed above 2026 and 2025; the contract names the one that applies. The numbers in UDOT's drainage pipe and backfill sections are not confirmed in this library because the files would not open; read the section in the contract's edition on UDOT's standards page or ask the UDOT Standards Coordinator. City, county and district utility work along the Wasatch Front usually follows the APWA Utah Chapter Manual of Standard Specifications and Plans with local amendments, not the UDOT book.",S,U,'2027 listed','low')

U='https://www.oregon.gov/odot/Business/Specs/2024_STANDARD_SPECIFICATIONS.pdf'
S='Oregon Standard Specifications for Construction, 2024 (ODOT/APWA Oregon Chapter), Sections 00405, 00406, 00445, 00470, 00490 (read 2026-11-20)'
add('spec-or-bore-1','OR','Oregon ODOT 2024 book: effective date, video speed, boring and jacking, adjusting manholes',
"Oregon (2024 Oregon Standard Specifications for Construction). This edition applies to ODOT projects bid on or after Dec. 1, 2023, and many cities use it with their own special provisions. Trench width at the surface is as narrow as practical but not less than 24 inches (00405.41(c)); the pipe zone runs to at least 8 inches over the pipe (00405.02); trench backfill is 95 percent of AASHTO T 99 under roadway and shoulders and 90 percent elsewhere (00405.46(c)(2)). Video inspection: the camera moves no faster than 30 feet per minute while recording (00445.74). Deflection mandrel: at least 9 vanes, 95 percent of the pipe's initial inside diameter, not less than 30 days after backfill (00445.73(c)). Tunneling, boring and jacking (Section 00406): pipe, casing or sleeves are jacked or bored to the required line and grade, and jacked casings 36 inches and larger get grout nipples at 10-foot centers when pressure grouting is specified (00406.12). Manhole vacuum test: 10 inches of mercury, timed to 9 inches (00470.71(b)). Adjusting structures (00490.46): no more than 24 inches from the new frame grade to the top of the cone.",S,U,'2024')

U='https://www.westlakepipe.com/sites/default/files/2024-10/mu-ig-003-us-en-0724.1_astm-d3034.pdf'
S='Westlake Pipe & Fittings, ASTM D3034 PVC Gravity Sewer Pipe Installation Guide, MU-IG-003-US-EN-0724.1, 2024 (our summary; read 2026-11-20)'
add('mfr-westlake-sewer-1','US','PVC gravity sewer pipe (SDR 35): cover before traffic, joint deflection and bending limits (Westlake guide)',
"PVC gravity sewer pipe (ASTM D3034), summarized from Westlake Pipe's 2024 installation guide. Embedment follows ASTM D2321 Classes I to IV. Cover before traffic crosses: 24 inches or one pipe diameter, whichever is larger, with Class I (crushed rock) embedment; 36 inches or one pipe diameter with Classes II to IV; 48 inches before a hydrohammer is used over the pipe. Flotation: about 1.5 pipe diameters of cover for SDR 32.5 and heavier pipe. Deflection: the guide uses 7.5 percent maximum at 30 days (ASTM D3034 appendix), checked with a go/no-go mandrel after 30 days; many agencies specify 5 percent. Joints: clean, lubricate the spigot bevel and gasket, keep the lengths straight, push with bar and block until the bell edge is on the insertion line, and do not over-insert. Joint deflection for this pipe is 1 degree: about 2.9 inches of offset on a 14-foot length and 4.2 inches on a 20-foot length. Bending the barrel by hand instead: minimum radius about 35 feet for 4 inch, 52 feet for 6 inch, 70 feet for 8 inch, 85 feet for 10 inch, 104 feet for 12 inch and 128 feet for 15 inch; not recommended above 15 inch; never bend and deflect the same length. Low-pressure air testing follows ASTM F1417. Laying lengths are 14 and 20 feet.",S,U,'2024')
